WEBVTT

NOTE Prepared from local speech recognition and editorial correction; Chinese editorial translation. Some name spellings are provisional and need family-source review.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.320 line:10% size:90%
The lineage of the Wu family begins with the ancient Ji surname.

2
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:09.760 line:10% size:90%
Their founding ancestor, Taibo, yielded an empire three times to his younger brother,

3
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.960 line:10% size:90%
an act of humility that secured his place in history.

4
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.040 line:10% size:90%
By the Song dynasty, descendants of this line had migrated south,

5
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.680 line:10% size:90%
tracing the Huanglong River into the Fujian region.

6
00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:26.540 line:10% size:90%
In 1376, a man named Wu Shen settled at the foot of Aofeng Mountain.

7
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.200 line:10% size:90%
He established the Guzhai branch of the family,

8
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.860 line:10% size:90%
planting a geographical root that would hold fast for over six centuries.

9
00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:38.740 line:10% size:90%
Across those 600 years, more than 20 generations meticulously recorded

10
00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:43.900 line:10% size:90%
every birth, death and migration into heavy physical genealogies.

11
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:50.000 line:10% size:90%
A family's identity and virtues only survive as long as the physical medium used to record them endures.

12
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:56.600 line:10% size:90%
Right now, the first generation of modern wealth creators in this family are between 60 and 80 years old.

13
00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:01.360 line:10% size:90%
Their minds hold unrecorded oral histories, the early business philosophies,

14
00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.500 line:10% size:90%
and memories of cross-border migrations.

15
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:08.140 line:10% size:90%
Once they pass, those specific voices and decisions vanish completely.

16
00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:11.440 line:10% size:90%
The physical records left behind are already degrading.

17
00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:17.560 line:10% size:90%
A genealogy book printed in 1932 sits with crumbling edges, its pages eaten by insects,

18
00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:20.120 line:10% size:90%
taking entire family branches with them.

19
00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:22.760 line:10% size:90%
The window to capture this data is closing.

20
00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:30.600 line:10% size:90%
Relying on static, one-off physical preservation ensures the eventual erasure of a 600-year legacy.

21
00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:36.640 line:10% size:90%
To read these genealogies is to see the exact cultural DNA of the Wu family.

22
00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:41.280 line:10% size:90%
They define their core ethos as Zhide, supreme virtue.

23
00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:46.000 line:10% size:90%
During the Ming dynasty, Wu Zishu built a fortress to protect his village from bandits.

24
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:52.000 line:10% size:90%
To negotiate the safety of his neighbors, he offered himself as a hostage and was killed in the enemy camp,

25
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:56.000 line:10% size:90%
cementing a family tradition of absolute loyalty.

26
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:04.000 line:10% size:90%
Centuries later, in the Qing dynasty, a 28-year-old widow named Lin-shi raised her son alone through extreme poverty.

27
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:09.400 line:10% size:90%
Her dedication earned her a royal chastity arch from the imperial court.

28
00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:15.600 line:10% size:90%
In the early Republic, Wu Ruiyu joined the revolutionary Tongmenghui to fight against warlords.

29
00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:21.760 line:10% size:90%
He died in combat, and his spiritual tablet still receives offerings in the ancestral hall today.

30
00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:24.280 line:10% size:90%
These are not myths passed down through hearsay.

31
00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:32.280 line:10% size:90%
They are empirical, recorded data points, proving a continuous chain of character that requires meticulous preservation.

32
00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:37.440 line:10% size:90%
By the early twentieth century, economic pressure forced the Wu bloodline to scatter.

33
00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.720 line:10% size:90%
Families boarded ships for Nanyang, seeking survival in Southeast Asia.

34
00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:46.160 line:10% size:90%
They sustained their ties to Fujian entirely through fragile paper letters bundled with remittances,

35
00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:50.080 line:10% size:90%
shipped back across the ocean over decades.

36
00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:56.360 line:10% size:90%
By the mid-twentieth century, figures like Wu Hongyi in Singapore and Wu Hongbao in Indonesia

37
00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:00.920 line:10% size:90%
had built successful enterprises in dense, booming markets.

38
00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:04.160 line:10% size:90%
They channeled that wealth directly back to the village.

39
00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:07.040 line:10% size:90%
They funded the reconstruction of the Guzhai ancestral hall

40
00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:10.000 line:10% size:90%
and built the local Aofeng Elementary School.

41
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.720 line:10% size:90%
In the modern era, that economic drive shifted to Shenzhen,

42
00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:16.840 line:10% size:90%
where the Wu brothers founded the Jida Industrial Group.

43
00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:21.120 line:10% size:90%
Their factories generate over 600 million RMB annually.

44
00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:28.760 line:10% size:90%
By prioritizing Guzhai locals for thousands of jobs, they engineered a complete economic turnaround for their home village.

45
00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:34.040 line:10% size:90%
Global dispersion did not break the Wu family, but it stretched the limits of physical paper and stone,

46
00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:41.040 line:10% size:90%
requiring a technological mechanism to track a legacy operating across multiple time zones.

47
00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:46.640 line:10% size:90%
DeepFamily approaches the monumental task of heritage preservation not just as an archive,

48
00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:50.580 line:10% size:90%
but as a rigorous, forward-looking digital engineering project.

49
00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:55.700 line:10% size:90%
Physical artifacts, century-old letters and raw oral histories are scanned

50
00:03:55.700 --> 00:04:01.380 line:10% size:90%
and broken apart into distinct data nodes, categorized by date, person and location.

51
00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:07.180 line:10% size:90%
Those nodes pass through a strictly governed system, sorted into one of four buckets: confirmed,

52
00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.900 line:10% size:90%
pending, family statement, or AI-inferred.

53
00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:16.000 line:10% size:90%
When historical memories conflict, the system merges them into a single timeline event,

54
00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.000 line:10% size:90%
securing the exact source citation for every claim.

55
00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:26.000 line:10% size:90%
A fragile stack of decaying paper becomes a mathematically verifiable, fully searchable knowledge base.

56
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:31.000 line:10% size:90%
The final result is a living digital ancestral hall,

57
00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:36.520 line:10% size:90%
a secure system operating continuously in the cloud for the global diaspora.

58
00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:42.080 line:10% size:90%
A modern descendant sitting in a Singapore office or a Shenzhen factory can instantly

59
00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:47.120 line:10% size:90%
pull up the exact archival evidence of their great-grandfather's migration.

60
00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:51.400 line:10% size:90%
The stone ancestral hall in Fujian requires a physical pilgrimage.

61
00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:57.280 line:10% size:90%
The digital ecosystem offers instantaneous, limitless access, updating in real time

62
00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:59.800 line:10% size:90%
as new data is verified.

63
00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:02.360 line:10% size:90%
Data endures for a century.

64
00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:04.800 line:10% size:90%
Models iterate for a century.

65
00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.000 line:10% size:90%
Through this digital transformation,

66
00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:13.180 line:10% size:90%
the Wu family legacy secures its place in the future.
